wopr: the WOPR computer from WarGames (1983), in your terminal.

Usage:
  wopr [flags] [game]
  wopr --movie [scene]

Flags:
  -v, --version                print the version and exit
  -h, --help                   print this help and exit
  -g, --games                  list the games and exit
  -S, --scenes                 list the movie's scenes and exit
  -L, --licenses               print licence notices and exit
  -p, --play <game>            start a game: number, name, alias or prefix
  -m, --movie                  replay the film's WOPR scenes from [scene] on
  -t, --theme <name>           imsai, green, amber, norad (env WOPR_THEME)
  -i, --instant                no typewriter pacing (env WOPR_INSTANT)
  -s, --seed <n>               deterministic run with this seed
  -r, --reduce-motion          no blinking or motion (env WOPR_REDUCE_MOTION)

At the LOGON: prompt, the film's backdoor still works: Joshua.
Type LOGOFF to leave. Ctrl+C quits at any time.

Movie mode plays the film's scenes from the one named to the end, then exits;
without one, it opens a menu of scenes. Space pauses, n or Right skips a scene,
p or Left goes back, and Esc opens the menu.

Examples:
  wopr                 dial in and log on
  wopr chess -i        play chess with no typewriter pacing
  wopr --games         list the games
  wopr -m 2            replay the film from scene 2 (wopr --scenes lists them)
